\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par  \cf0 1. O God, our help in ages past,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Our hope for years to come,
\par Our shelter from the stormy blast,
\par And our eternal home!
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2. Under the shadow of Thy throne
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Thy saints have dwelt secure;
\par Sufficient is Thine arm alone,
\par And our defence is sure.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3.  Before the hills in order stood,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 Or earth received her frame,
\par From everlasting Thou art God,
\par To endless years the same.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4.  A thousand ages in Thy sight
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Are like an evening gone;
\par Short as the watch that ends the night
\par Before the rising sun.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  5.   Time, like an ever-rolling stream,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0 Bears all its sons away;
\par They fly forgotten, as a dream
\par Dies at the opening day.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-270\li315\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  6. O God, our help in ages past,
\par \pard\li315\sl190\slmult0\qj Our hope for years to come,
\par Be Thou our guard while troubles last,
\par \pard     And our eternal home.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

